mpv: add the objc language where Apple .m sources are added

mpv 0.41.0 only calls add_languages(objc) when it detects a macOS SDK.
An iOS cross build (ao_audiounit.m) or a cocoa build can miss that, so add
objc where the .m files are added. Inherited fix, ported to 0.41.0.
Drop when upstream adds objc for iOS builds itself.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index fb10be5..58f57bd 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -412,6 +412,7 @@ cocoa = dependency('appleframeworks', modules: ['Cocoa', 'IOKit', 'QuartzCore'],
                    required: get_option('cocoa'))
 features += {'cocoa': cocoa.found()}
 if features['cocoa']
+    add_languages('objc')
     dependencies += cocoa
     path_source += files('osdep/path-mac.m')
     sources += files('osdep/language-mac.c',
@@ -811,6 +812,7 @@ audiounit = {
 }
 features += {'audiounit': audiounit['deps'].found() and audiounit['symbol']}
 if features['audiounit']
+    add_languages('objc')
     dependencies += audiounit['deps']
     sources += files('audio/out/ao_audiounit.m')
 endif
